{
  "about": "Golden vectors of the meta value at the key 'horizon/last', and of the Horizon a store reports from it and the four layers' stored horizons. A horizon is stored as time.Time's binary form (version byte 1, seconds since year 1 as 8 bytes big endian, nanoseconds as 4, the zone offset in minutes as 2, 0xffff for UTC) then its Seq as 8 bytes big endian; the key holds exactly that encoding. The value is trusted only if it equals one of the layers' stored horizons and its Seq is the largest among them; otherwise Horizon is the stored layer horizon with the largest Seq and, among those, the latest time. A layer that was never retained has no key, which stands for the zero horizon. The expectations were computed independently of the code.",
  "key": "00686f72697a6f6e2f6c617374",
